\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come let us sing of a wonderful love,
\par Tender and true;
\par Out of the heart of the Father above,
\par Streaming to me and to you:
\par Wonderful love
\par Dwells in the heart of the father above.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Jesus, the Saviour, this gospel to tell,
\par Joyfully came;
\par Came with the helpless and 
\par hopeless to dwell,
\par Sharing their sorrow and shame;
\par Seeking the lost,
\par Saving, redeeming at measureless cost.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Jesus is seeking the wanderers yet;
\par Why do they roam?
\par Love only waits to forgive and forget;
\par Home! weary wanderers, home!
\par Wonderful love
\par Dwells in the heart of the father above.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Come to my heart, O Thou wonderful love,
\par Come and abide,
\par Lifting my life till it rises above
\par Envy and falsehood and pride ;
\par Seeking to be
\par Lowly and humble, a learner of Thee.\f1 
\par 
\par }

